  "id": "weber-fraction",
  "term": "Weber fraction",
  "definition": "The Weber fraction is a measure of sensitivity to differences in magnitude, meaning the smallest change needed to notice that two amounts differ. In research on approximate number perception, its value can vary a lot depending on the task and method used, so it should not be treated as a context-free measure.",
